course: dictionary
lesson: 11587
title: Words that fight germs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Microbes are tiny living things that are far too small to see without a microscope. Some microbes are bacteria, some are viruses, and some are fungi. Most are harmless, but some make us ill. The word antimicrobial is built from three parts: anti means against, micro means tiny, and bio means living. So antimicrobial means against tiny living things.
explain: «The nurse washed her hands with antimicrobial soap.» Here antimicrobial is an adjective, a word that describes the soap. It tells you the soap kills or stops the growth of germs. Ask yourself: what does the soap do to the germs? If it kills them, the word fits.
explain: «Doctors gave Sam an antimicrobial medicine to stop the bacteria making him ill.» Here the word is a noun, the name of a thing. An antimicrobial is a medicine or substance that kills microbes or stops them growing. Antibiotics are one kind of antimicrobial, so when you see an antibiotic in a science lesson, you can call it an antimicrobial too.
fact: Antimicrobial means killing or stopping the growth of microbes.
fact: Microbes are tiny living things such as bacteria, viruses and fungi.
fact: «Antimicrobial» can be an adjective, as in «antimicrobial soap», or a noun, as in «an antimicrobial».
fact: Antibiotics are antimicrobials, and so are some soaps and sprays.
fact: Antimicrobial resistance means microbes change so that a medicine no longer works against them.
exercise: «The nurse washed her hands with antimicrobial soap.» What does antimicrobial mean here? | Warm and soapy | *Killing or stopping tiny germs | Making hands smell nice | Made of cotton
exercise: What are microbes? | *Tiny living things such as bacteria and fungi | Big animals that live in the sea | Pieces of metal used in machines | Types of soap
exercise: «Antibiotics are antimicrobials that stop bacteria growing.» Which of these is an antimicrobial? | A cotton sock | A glass window | *An antibiotic tablet | A bicycle wheel
test: «Doctors used an antimicrobial medicine to stop the infection spreading.» What is an antimicrobial? | A type of hospital bed | Something that helps germs grow | A tiny bacteria that makes people ill | *A medicine or substance that kills microbes or stops them growing
test: «Antimicrobial resistance is making some medicines less useful.» What does antimicrobial resistance mean? | *When microbes change so a medicine stops working against them | When a soap smells very strong | When a medicine becomes cheaper | When hands are too clean to need washing
exam: Which is the best example of an antimicrobial? | A fluffy towel | *A medicine that kills bacteria | A pencil case | A glass of water
